msgstr ""
"Modifie à distance de la valeur de la propriété indiquée par [code]peer_id[/"
"code] (voir [method NetworkedMultiplayerPeer.set_target_peer])."

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the channel to use is set for this [MultiplayerPeer] (see "
"[member MultiplayerPeer.transfer_channel])."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/MultiplayerPeerExtension.xml
msgid ""
"Called when the transfer mode is set on this [MultiplayerPeer] (see [member "
"MultiplayerPeer.transfer_mode])."
msgstr ""

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Automatically replicates spawnable nodes from the authority to other "
"multiplayer peers."
msgstr ""
"Réplique automatiquement les nœuds spawnables de l'autorité sur les autres "
"pairs multijoueurs."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Spawnable scenes can be configured in the editor or through code (see "
"[method add_spawnable_scene]).\n"
"Also supports custom node spawns through [method spawn], calling [member "
"spawn_function] on all peers.\n"
"Internally, [MultiplayerSpawner] uses [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_add] to notify spawns passing the "
"spawned node as the [code]object[/code] and itself as the "
"[code]configuration[/code], and [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_remove] to notify despawns in a similar "
"way."
msgstr ""
"Les scènes spawnables peuvent être configurées dans l'éditeur ou via le code "
"(voir [method add_spawnable_scene]).\n"
"Supporte également le spawn de nœuds personnalisés via [method spawn], en "
"appelant [member spawn_function] sur tous les pairs.\n"
"En interne, [MultiplayerSpawner] utilise [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_add] pour notifier des spawns en passant "
"le nœud spawné dans [code]object[/code] et lui-même dans "
"[code]configuration[/code], et [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_remove] pour notifier des despawns de "
"manière similaire."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a scene path to spawnable scenes, making it automatically replicated "
"from the multiplayer authority to other peers when added as children of the "
"node pointed by [member spawn_path]."
msgstr ""
"Ajoute un chemin de scène aux scènes spawnables, la rendant automatiquement "
"répliquée de l'autorité multijoueur vers d'autres pairs lorsqu'elle est "
"ajoutée comme enfant du nœud pointé par [member spawn_path]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Clears all spawnable scenes. Does not despawn existing instances on remote "
"peers."
msgstr ""
"Efface toutes les scènes spawnables. Ne despawn pas les instances existantes "
"sur les pairs distants."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid "Returns the spawnable scene path by index."
msgstr "Renvoie le chemin d'une scène spawnable par index."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid "Returns the count of spawnable scene paths."
msgstr "Renvoie le nombre de chemins de scènes spawnables."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Requests a custom spawn, with [param data] passed to [member spawn_function] "
"on all peers. Returns the locally spawned node instance already inside the "
"scene tree, and added as a child of the node pointed by [member "
"spawn_path].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Spawnable scenes are spawned automatically. [method spawn] is "
"only needed for custom spawns."
msgstr ""
"Demande un spawn personnalisé, avec [param data] passée à [member "
"spawn_function] sur tous les pairs. Renvoie l'instance du nœud spawné "
"localement déjà à l'intérieur de l’arborescence de scène, et ajouté en tant "
"qu'enfant du nœud pointé par [member spawn_path].\n"
"[b]Note :[/b] Les scènes spawnables sont générées automatiquement. [method "
"spawn] n'est nécessaire que pour les spawns personnalisés."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Method called on all peers when a custom [method spawn] is requested by the "
"authority. Will receive the [code]data[/code] parameter, and should return a "
"[Node] that is not in the scene tree.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The returned node should [b]not[/b] be added to the scene with "
"[method Node.add_child]. This is done automatically."
msgstr ""
"Méthode appelée sur tous les pairs quand un [method spawn] personnalisé est "
"demandé par l'autorité. Recevra le paramètre [code]data[/code] et devrait "
"renvoyer un [Node] qui n'est pas dans l'arborescence de scène.\n"
"[b]Note :[/b] Le nœud renvoyé ne devrait [b]pas[/b] être ajouté à la scène "
"avec [method Node.add_child]. Ceci est fait automatiquement."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Maximum number of nodes allowed to be spawned by this spawner. Includes both "
"spawnable scenes and custom spawns.\n"
"When set to [code]0[/code] (the default), there is no limit."
msgstr ""
"Nombre maximal de nœuds autorisés à être spawnés par ce spawner. Comprend "
"des scènes spawnables et des spawns personnalisés.\n"
"Lorsque défini à [code]0[/code] (par défaut), il n'y a pas de limite."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Path to the spawn root. Spawnable scenes that are added as direct children "
"are replicated to other peers."
msgstr ""
"Chemin vers la racine de spawn. Les scènes spawnables qui sont ajoutées "
"comme enfants directs sont répliquées sur les autres pairs."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a spawnable scene or custom spawn was despawned by the "
"multiplayer authority. Only called on remote peers."
msgstr ""
"Émis lorsqu'une scène spawnable ou un spawn personnalisé a été despawn par "
"l'autorité multijoueur. Seulement appelée sur les pairs distants."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSpawner.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a spawnable scene or custom spawn was spawned by the "
"multiplayer authority. Only called on remote peers."
msgstr ""
"Émis lorsqu'une scène spawnable ou un spawn personnalisé a été spawn par "
"l'autorité multijoueur. Seulement appelée sur les pairs distants."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Synchronizes properties from the multiplayer authority to the remote peers."
msgstr ""
"Synchronise des propriétés de l'autorité multijoueur vers les pairs distants."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"By default, [MultiplayerSynchronizer] synchronizes configured properties to "
"all peers.\n"
"Visibility can be handled directly with [method set_visibility_for] or as-"
"needed with [method add_visibility_filter] and [method update_visibility].\n"
"[MultiplayerSpawner]s will handle nodes according to visibility of "
"synchronizers as long as the node at [member root_path] was spawned by one.\n"
"Internally, [MultiplayerSynchronizer] uses [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_add] to notify synchronization start "
"passing the [Node] at [member root_path] as the [code]object[/code] and "
"itself as the [code]configuration[/code], and uses [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_remove] to notify synchronization end in "
"a similar way.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Synchronization is not supported for [Object] type properties, "
"like [Resource]. Properties that are unique to each peer, like the instance "
"IDs of [Object]s (see [method Object.get_instance_id]) or [RID]s, will also "
"not work in synchronization."
msgstr ""
"Par défaut, [MultiplayerSynchronizer] synchronise les propriétés configurées "
"vers tous les pairs.\n"
"La visibilité peut être gérée directement avec [method set_visibility_for] "
"ou au besoin avec [method add_visibility_filter] et [method "
"update_visibility].\n"
"Les [MultiplayerSpawner]s géreront les nœuds en fonction de la visibilité "
"des synchroniseurs tant que le nœud à [member root_path] ait été spawné par "
"un MultiplayerSpawner..\n"
"En interne, [MultiplayerSynchronizer] utilise [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_add] pour notifier le démarrage de la "
"synchronisation en passant [Node] à [member root_path] dans [code]object[/"
"code] et lui-même dans [code]configuration[/code], et utilise [method "
"MultiplayerAPI.object_configuration_remove] pour notifier la fin de la "
"synchronisation de la même manière.\n"
"[b]Note :[/b] La synchronisation n'est pas supportée pour les propriétés de "
"type [Object], comme [Resource]. Les propriétés qui sont uniques à chaque "
"pair, comme les identifiants d'instance d'[Object]s (voir [method "
"Object.get_instance_id]) ou les [RID]s, ne fonctionneront aussi pas dans la "
"synchronisation."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a peer visibility filter for this synchronizer.\n"
"[param filter] should take a peer ID [int] and return a [bool]."
msgstr ""
"Ajoute un filtre de visibilité des pairs pour ce synchroniseur.\n"
"[param filter] devrait prendre un identifiant [int] de pair et renvoyer un "
"[bool]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Queries the current visibility for peer [param peer]."
msgstr "Demande la visibilité actuelle du pair [param peer]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Removes a peer visibility filter from this synchronizer."
msgstr "Retire un filtre de visibilité des pairs de ce synchroniseur."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Sets the visibility of [param peer] to [param visible]. If [param peer] is "
"[code]0[/code], the value of [member public_visibility] will be updated "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Définit la visibilité du pair [param peer] à [param visible]. Si [param "
"peer] vaut [code]0[/code], la valeur de [member public_visibility] sera mise "
"à jour à la place."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Updates the visibility of [param for_peer] according to visibility filters. "
"If [param for_peer] is [code]0[/code] (the default), all peers' visibilties "
"are updated."
msgstr ""
"Met à jour la visibilité de [param for_peer] selon les filtres de "
"visibilité. Si [param for_peer] vaut [code]0[/code] (par défaut), toutes les "
"visibilités des pairs sont mises à jour."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Time interval between delta synchronizations. Used when the replication is "
"set to [constant SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ON_CHANGE]. If set "
"to [code]0.0[/code] (the default), delta synchronizations happen every "
"network process frame."
msgstr ""
"Intervalle de temps entre les synchronisations delta. Utilisé lorsque la "
"réplication est définie à [constant "
"SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ON_CHANGE]. Si défini à [code]0.0[/"
"code] (la valeur par défaut), les synchronisations delta se produisent à "
"chaque trame de traitement réseau."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Whether synchronization should be visible to all peers by default. See "
"[method set_visibility_for] and [method add_visibility_filter] for ways of "
"configuring fine-grained visibility options."
msgstr ""
"Indique si la synchronisation devrait être visible par défaut pour tous les "
"pairs. Voir [method set_visibility_for] et [method add_visibility_filter] "
"pour des moyens de configurer des options de visibilité plus détaillées."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Resource containing which properties to synchronize."
msgstr "Ressource contenant les propriétés à synchroniser."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Time interval between synchronizations. Used when the replication is set to "
"[constant SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ALWAYS]. If set to "
"[code]0.0[/code] (the default), synchronizations happen every network "
"process frame."
msgstr ""
"Intervalle de temps entre les synchronisations. Utilisé lorsque la "
"réplication est définie à [constant "
"SceneReplicationConfig.REPLICATION_MODE_ALWAYS]. Si défini à [code]0.0[/"
"code] (la valeur par défaut), les synchronisations se produisent à chaque "
"trame de traitement réseau."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Node path that replicated properties are relative to.\n"
"If [member root_path] was spawned by a [MultiplayerSpawner], the node will "
"be also be spawned and despawned based on this synchronizer visibility "
"options."
msgstr ""
"Chemin du nœud auquel les propriétés répliquées sont relatives.\n"
"Si [member root_path] a été spawné par un [MultiplayerSpawner], le nœud sera "
"également spawné et despawné en fonction des options de visibilité de ce "
"synchroniseur."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid "Specifies when visibility filters are updated."
msgstr "Spécifie quand les filtres de visibilité sont mis à jour."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a new delta synchronization state is received by this "
"synchronizer after the properties have been updated."
msgstr ""
"Émis quand un nouvel état de synchronisation delta est reçu par ce "
"synchroniseur après que les propriétés aient été mises à jour."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when a new synchronization state is received by this synchronizer "
"after the properties have been updated."
msgstr ""
"Émis quand un nouvel état de synchronisation est reçu par ce synchroniseur "
"après que les propriétés aient été mises à jour."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Emitted when visibility of [param for_peer] is updated. See [method "
"update_visibility]."
msgstr ""
"Émis quand la visibilité du pair [param for_peer] est mise à jour. Voir "
"[method update_visibility]."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Visibility filters are updated during process frames (see [constant "
"Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PROCESS])."
msgstr ""
"Les filtres de visibilité sont mis à jour pendant les trames de traitement "
"(voir [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PROCESS])."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Visibility filters are updated during physics frames (see [constant "
"Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS])."
msgstr ""
"Les filtres de visibilité sont mis à jour pendant les trames de physique "
"(voir [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS])."

#: modules/multiplayer/doc_classes/MultiplayerSynchronizer.xml
msgid ""
"Visibility filters are not updated automatically, and must be updated "
"manually by calling [method update_visibility]."
msgstr ""
"Les filtres de visibilité ne sont pas mis à jour automatiquement et doivent "
"être mis à jour manuellement en appelant [method update_visibility]."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid "A binary [Semaphore] for synchronization of multiple [Thread]s."
msgstr "Un [Semaphore] binaire pour la synchronisation de plusieurs [Thread]s."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A synchronization mutex (mutual exclusion). This is used to synchronize "
"multiple [Thread]s, and is equivalent to a binary [Semaphore]. It guarantees "
"that only one thread can access a critical section at a time.\n"
"This is a reentrant mutex, meaning that it can be locked multiple times by "
"one thread, provided it also unlocks it as many times.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] To ensure proper cleanup without crashes or deadlocks, the "
"following conditions must be met:\n"
"- When a [Mutex]'s reference count reaches zero and it is therefore "
"destroyed, no threads (including the one on which the destruction will "
"happen) must have it locked.\n"
"- When a [Thread]'s reference count reaches zero and it is therefore "
"destroyed, it must not have any mutex locked."
msgstr ""
"Un mutex (MUTual EXclusion, litt \"exclusion mutuelle\") de synchronisation. "
"Ceci est utilisé pour synchroniser plusieurs [Thread]s, et est équivalent à "
"un [Semaphore] binaire. Il garantit qu'un seul thread peut accéder à une "
"section critique à la fois.\n"
"Il s'agit un mutex ré-entrant, ce qui signifie qu'il peut être verrouillé "
"plusieurs fois par un thread, à condition qu'il est déverrouillé autant de "
"fois.\n"
"[b]Attention :[/b] Les mutex doivent être utilisés soigneusement pour éviter "
"des blocages.\n"
"[b]Attention :[/b] Pour assurer un nettoyage approprié sans crash ni "
"blocages, les conditions suivantes doivent être remplies :\n"
"- Lorsque le nombre de référence d'un [Mutex] atteint zéro et qu'il est donc "
"détruit, aucun thread (y compris celui sur lequel la destruction se "
"produira) ne doit l'avoir verrouillé.\n"
"- Lorsque le nombre de référence d'un [Thread] atteint zéro et qu'il est "
"donc détruit, il ne doit pas avoir de mutex verrouillé."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml doc/classes/Semaphore.xml doc/classes/Thread.xml
#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid "Using multiple threads"
msgstr "Utiliser plusieurs fils d'exécution"

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml doc/classes/Semaphore.xml doc/classes/Thread.xml
#: doc/classes/WorkerThreadPool.xml
msgid "Thread-safe APIs"
msgstr "Les API sûres pour plusieurs fils d'exécution"

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid ""
"Locks this [Mutex], blocks until it is unlocked by the current owner.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function returns without blocking if the thread already "
"has ownership of the mutex."
msgstr ""
"Verrouille ce [Mutex], le bloque jusqu'à ce qu'il soit déverrouillé par le "
"propriétaire actuel.\n"
"[b]Note :[/b] Cette fonction renvoie sans bloquer si ce thread est déjà le "
"propriétaire du mutex."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
msgid ""
"Tries locking this [Mutex], but does not block. Returns [code]true[/code] on "
"success, [code]false[/code] otherwise.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This function returns [code]true[/code] if the thread already "
"has ownership of the mutex."
msgstr ""
"Essaie de verrouiller ce [Mutex], mais ne le bloque pas. Renvoie [code]true[/"
"code] en cas de succès, [code]false[/code] sinon.\n"
"[b]Note :[/b] Cette fonction renvoie [code]true[/code] si le thread possède "
"déjà le mutex."

#: doc/classes/Mutex.xml
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Unlocks this [Mutex], leaving it to other threads.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] If a thread called [method lock] or [method try_lock] multiple "
"times while already having ownership of the mutex, it must also call [method "
"unlock] the same number of times in order to unlock it correctly.\n"
"[b]Warning:[/b] Calling [method unlock] more times than [method lock] on a "
"given thread, thus ending up trying to unlock a non-locked mutex, is wrong "
"and may causes crashes or deadlocks."
msgstr ""
"Déverrouille ce [Mutex], le laissant à d'autres threads.\n"
"[b]Note :[/b] Si un thread a appelé [method lock] ou [method try_lock] "
"plusieurs fois en étant déjà propriétaire du mutex, il doit également "
"appeler [method unlock] autant de fois pour le déverrouiller correctement.\n"
"[b]Attention :[/b] Appeler [method unlock] plus de fois que [method lock] "
"sur un thread donné, se terminant ainsi en essayant de déverrouiller un "
"mutex non verrouillé, est incorrect et peut causer des plantages ou des "
"blocages."

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid "A server interface for OS native menus."
msgstr "Une interface serveur pour les menus natifs d'OS."

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"[NativeMenu] handles low-level access to the OS native global menu bar and "
"popup menus.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This is low-level API, consider using [MenuBar] with [member "
"MenuBar.prefer_global_menu] set to [code]true[/code], and [PopupMenu] with "
"[member PopupMenu.prefer_native_menu] set to [code]true[/code].\n"
"To create a menu, use [method create_menu], add menu items using "
"[code]add_*_item[/code] methods. To remove a menu, use [method free_menu].\n"
"[codeblock]\n"
"var menu\n"
"\n"
"func _menu_callback(item_id):\n"
"\tif item_id == \"ITEM_CUT\":\n"
"\t\tcut()\n"
"\telif item_id == \"ITEM_COPY\":\n"
"\t\tcopy()\n"
"\telif item_id == \"ITEM_PASTE\":\n"
"\t\tpaste()\n"
"\n"
"func _enter_tree():\n"
"\t# Create new menu and add items:\n"
"\tmenu = NativeMenu.create_menu()\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_item(menu, \"Cut\", _menu_callback, Callable(), "
"\"ITEM_CUT\")\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_item(menu, \"Copy\", _menu_callback, Callable(), "
"\"ITEM_COPY\")\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_separator(menu)\n"
"\tNativeMenu.add_item(menu, \"Paste\", _menu_callback, Callable(), "
"\"ITEM_PASTE\")\n"
"\n"
"func _on_button_pressed():\n"
"\t# Show popup menu at mouse position:\n"
"\tNativeMenu.popup(menu, DisplayServer.mouse_get_position())\n"
"\n"
"func _exit_tree():\n"
"\t# Remove menu when it's no longer needed:\n"
"\tNativeMenu.free_menu(menu)\n"
"[/codeblock]"
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new checkable item with text [param label] to the global menu [param "
"rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new checkable item with text [param label] and icon [param icon] to "
"the global menu [param rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new item with text [param label] and icon [param icon] to the global "
"menu [param rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new radio-checkable item with text [param label] and icon [param "
"icon] to the global menu [param rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Radio-checkable items just display a checkmark, but don't have "
"any built-in checking behavior and must be checked/unchecked manually. See "
"[method set_item_checked] for more info on how to control it.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new item with text [param label] to the global menu [param rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new item with text [param label] to the global menu [param rid].\n"
"Contrarily to normal binary items, multistate items can have more than two "
"states, as defined by [param max_states]. Each press or activate of the item "
"will increase the state by one. The default value is defined by [param "
"default_state].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] By default, there's no indication of the current item state, it "
"should be changed manually.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: doc/classes/NativeMenu.xml
msgid ""
"Adds a new radio-checkable item with text [param label] to the global menu "
"[param rid].\n"
"Returns index of the inserted item, it's not guaranteed to be the same as "
"[param index] value.\n"
"An [param accelerator] can optionally be defined, which is a keyboard "
"shortcut that can be pressed to trigger the menu button even if it's not "
"currently open. The [param accelerator] is generally a combination of [enum "
"KeyModifierMask]s and [enum Key]s using bitwise OR such as "
"[code]KEY_MASK_CTRL | KEY_A[/code] ([kbd]Ctrl + A[/kbd]).\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] Radio-checkable items just display a checkmark, but don't have "
"any built-in checking behavior and must be checked/unchecked manually. See "
"[method set_item_checked] for more info on how to control it.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] The [param callback] and [param key_callback] Callables need to "
"accept exactly one Variant parameter, the parameter passed to the Callables "
"will be the value passed to [param tag].\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] This method is implemented on macOS and Windows.\n"
"[b]Note:[/b] On Windows, [param accelerator] and [param key_callback] are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

